            <abstract>
                <p>Qǝne of probably rather old origin. The type is indicated in the manuscript <ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/Sahleka">śāhlǝka</ref>, which is not mentioned in the classification 
                    by <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/C92MK42D"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Guidi1900Qene"/><title level="a">"Qenê" o inni abissini</title><title level="j">Atti della Reale Accademia dei Lincei, Rendiconti, Classe di scienze morale, storiche e filologiche</title><author><forename>Ignazio</forename><surname>Guidi</surname></author><date>1900</date><biblScope unit="volume">Serie quinta, 9</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">463-510</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">Hymns</note><note type="tag">Poetry</note><note type="tag">Prosody</note><note type="tag">bm:Guidi1900Qene</note></note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">Hymns</note><note type="tag">Poetry</note><note type="tag">Prosody</note><note type="tag">bm:Guidi1900Qene</note><citedRange unit="page">4-5</citedRange></bibl>, who instead described 
                    qǝne with three verses as <ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/Mibazhu">Mi-bazḫu-type</ref> or 
                    <ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/Zaamlakiya">Za-ʾamlākiya-type</ref>.</p>
            </abstract>
